# Supabase
#
# supabase/migrations/**.sql IS TRACKED ON PURPOSE. It was previously excluded by a
# global `*.sql` ignore, on the rationale that it "exposes the project ID". That
# rationale was wrong: the project ref is already committed in CLAUDE_CODE_BRIEF.md
# and HANDOFF_make_supabase_sync.md, is in git history, and ships in the deployed JS
# bundle next to the publishable anon key. A project ref is a public identifier, like
# a subdomain — every browser request contains it. Security here is RLS + key
# scoping, not obscurity. The genuinely sensitive files are named below.
#
# The cost of that ignore was real: zero migration history, so the live database was
# the only source of truth for DDL and RLS, and two tests were red because the
# migration/function files they read no longer existed.
supabase/config.toml
supabase/.env*
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/

# One-off SQL generated against real customer data (INSERTs with names/addresses)
scripts/import/**/*.sql
reset_jobs_from_sheets.sql

# Customer PII — every CSV/XLSX in this repo is real customer data from a one-time
# import. Keep the blanket ignore; add an explicit negation if a fixture is ever safe.
*.csv